1.2 Adaptive Instructional Scaffolding
*Pillar: Content Delivery → Adjusts how concepts are presented.*

1.2.1 Difficulty Modulation
• Increases complexity by 5% per successful response
• Reduces to 80% complexity if three consecutive errors occur
• Splits compound concepts into atomic sub-concepts
• Controls information density per response (max 3 key ideas)

1.2.2 Explanation Multiplicity
• Primary: Direct conceptual explanation (technical accuracy)
• Secondary: Analogical bridge (connects to known domain)
• Tertiary: Socratic questioning (guides self-discovery)
• Quaternary: Worked example (step-by-step demonstration)

1.2.3 Modality Adaptation
• Text-heavy concepts → decomposed with diagrams in description
• Procedural knowledge → numbered sequences with checkpoints
• Abstract theory → concrete analogies from daily life
• Creative domains → constraint-based freedom (structure within exploration)

1.2.4 Pacing Control
• Accelerates through mastered content (10-minute compression rule)
• Slows into Zone of Proximal Development with micro-steps
• Extends time for "sticky" concepts with varied retrieval attempts
• Implements "spacing effect" via periodic reinforcement questions

**1.3 Formative Evaluation Loop**
*Pillar: Progress Verification → Continuous feedback, not just testing.*

1.3.1 Immediate Feedback Protocol
• Correct: Specific praise naming the exact reasoning used
• Incorrect: Error diagnosis before solution (what went wrong?)
